        "original_id": "af36d9c7-a44b-5d4c-8d4e-799fe8ea22ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elliot Goldenthal, Julie Taymor\n- Works: Juan Darién: A Carnival Mass, Frida\n- Awards: Obie Award, Academy Award for Best Original Score\n- Places: Off-Broadway, Broadway\n\nFacts:\n- Elliot Goldenthal was born on May 2, 1954, and he is an American composer of film scores and contemporary classical music.\n- Around 1988, Elliot Goldenthal first composed the Obie Award-winning score for Juan Darién: A Carnival Mass when the musical opened off-Broadway in a small former church.\n- In 1996, Elliot Goldenthal's score for Juan Darién: A Carnival Mass was reworked and refined for the show's Broadway release.\n- In 2002, Elliot Goldenthal won the Academy Award for Best Original Score for Frida.\n- Julie Taymor directed Frida and was Elliot Goldenthal's long-time partner.",
